Strip the board to components and nets; add a guided routing document

Per the request to leave only what has to be connected, the delivered
board now contains the 33 footprints with their nets, the 90x90 mm
outline and the four M3 holes. No tracks, vias or zones.

- generate_routing_guide.py: reads the board and writes GUIA_ENRUTADO.md
  listing every net in routing order with its pads, their coordinates in
  mm, the recommended track width and a note per block. Multi-pad nets are
  chained by nearest neighbour so the suggested path flows.
- DESIGN.md: documents that routing is manual and why the A* autorouter
  was dropped.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
